  "conclusion": "Every bounded pre-target gate passed from the clean coordination commit, including all six canonical identities, seven Swift suites, 14 packaged dispatch tests, privacy, authorized-surface, fixture/production-surface, protected-evidence, and diff checks. The unchanged issue #110 controller launched the exact preserved candidate once, validated its candidate/session and zero-operation prerequisites, atomically published the owner-only marker, and entered the 120-second handoff with one declared owner focus action. Direct coordinator marker validation passed and the owner instruction was emitted immediately. Across 1,802 observations the controller did not detect the exact candidate becoming Accessibility or Workspace frontmost. Whether an owner click physically occurred is not established; the required focus transition was not detected. The controller stopped before raise or independent-observer execution, cleaned the marker, and terminated the candidate. Separate terminal checks found the marker and publication temporary absent and zero target processes. No GUI input by Codex, Computer Use, product action, fixture, sampler, artifact, destination, dispatch, measurement, issue #95 operation, or issue #104 consumption occurred. No retry or fallback is authorized; issue #104 remains unconsumed and a new owner decision is required."
